=== task: multi medium
title: Which jobs fit fast and slow?
prompt: Choose **every** job that fast and slow pointers, moving the same way, do well.
* Removing the repeats from a sorted list in place :: Right. slow keeps the last unique value; fast reads ahead.
* Moving the zeros to the end, keeping the order of the rest :: Right. slow marks where the next non-zero goes.
* Finding the middle of a linked list in one pass :: Right. fast moves two nodes, slow one.
* Detecting a loop in a linked list :: Right. fast catches slow inside the loop.
- Checking whether a word is a palindrome :: That compares the two ends: opposite pointers.
- Finding the two walls that hold the most water :: That's opposite pointers again.
hint: Same direction means both pointers start at the front.
hint: Which jobs need the front and the back at the same time instead?
right: The four in-place and linked-list jobs use same-direction pointers. Palindromes and the most water work from both ends inward.
wrong: Fast and slow pointers both start at the front: in-place removal, moving zeros, the middle and loop detection. Palindromes and water containers compare the two ends, which is the opposite-ends style.

